    "mixed-ground": [
      {
        "_comment": "Air and ground working the same hillside. An entry with no 'class' is an air multirotor, exactly as every preset above; 'class' names a VehicleClass and 'domain' is optional documentation that must agree with the class the server derives. 'headingDeg' is clockwise from true north. Staged on the west flank of the alpine preset's east peak, where the ground genuinely has grade: terrain runs 32-51 m here against a -3 m water surface, so nothing spawns afloat, and the rovers sit on 6.5, 23.8 and 6.7 degree slopes - inside every profile's climb and cross-slope limits, with the tracked rover close enough to its own to make the mobility assessment mean something. A ground entry's 'pos' Y is ignored: a rover's height is read off the terrain under its footprint.",
        "id": "mg-overwatch-1",
        "pos": [
          620.0,
          130.0,
          300.0
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "mg-overwatch-2",
