    "coastal-search": [
      {
        "_comment": "Maritime search on the 'coastal' terrain preset, which is the only preset whose water surface (+3.0 m) sits above the datum - SELECT THAT PRESET BEFORE RUNNING THIS SCENARIO. A preset places assets and never touches the environment, so run against the default 'alpine' terrain every vessel here is placed on a hillside and reports itself aground; it stays commandable, but the demo is meaningless. Staged in the channel west of the main island: the three vessels float in 5.5 m of water for 4.95 m of under-keel clearance against a 0.55 m draft and a 0.305 m advisory margin - comfortably clear, and every straight leg between them sweeps at least 5.2 m so a transit ordered from one to another is not refused for a shoal. The rovers are ashore on ground that is dry (14-17 m) and gentle (under 7 degrees), so both spawn drivable. A ground or surface entry's 'pos' Y is ignored: a rover's height is read off the terrain under its footprint and a vessel's is the water surface where it floats. External contacts are NOT spawned from a preset - a track is an observation, and POST /api/v2/sim/tracks is deliberately the only way one enters a session.",
